(150, 'Nob Hill Elementary', '2671', 1, 'Prevention School of Excellence In 2009 Nob Hill Elementary was one of only nine Broward County Schools awarded the Prevention School of Excellence Award.  The school was recognized for its outstanding effort in providing effective services, support, and activities that promote positive behaviors – development of emotional resilience skills, positive mental health, and prosocial actions – while limiting and/or preventing violent behavior and drug use.', '2025-12-11 08:40:00-04', null),
(150, 'Nob Hill Elementary', '2671', 2, '5 Star Award Nob Hill was also awarded the Five Star School Award that was created by the Commissioner’s Community Involvement Council of Florida and is presented annually to those schools that have shown evidence of exemplary community involvement. In order for a school to receive this award, a school must show documentation that it has achieved 100% of the established criteria in the categories of business partnerships, family involvement, volunteerism, Student Community Service, and School Advisory Councils.', '2025-12-11 08:40:00-04', null),
(150, 'Nob Hill Elementary', '2671', 3, 'Blue Ribbon School In 1992 Nob Hill Elementary was awarded the Blue Ribbon Award from the Secretary of Education for being high performing, regardless of the school’s demographics or percentage of students from disadvantaged backgrounds and for having reduced the achievement gap by improving student performance to high levels in reading and mathematics on state assessments or tests referenced by national norms.', '2025-12-11 08:40:00-04', null),
(150, 'Nob Hill Elementary', '2671', 4, 'A+ School For 12 years Nob Hill has been rated as an “A” school by the state of Florida through the A+School Recognition Funds.  This fund was set up by Florida’s former governor who proposed that a program be established that monies be awarded to schools that improved a letter grade or sustained high achievement.  The letter grades are determined by meeting certain high-performance levels on the FCAT (Florida Comprehensive Assessment Tests)', '2025-12-11 08:40:00-04', null),
(151, 'New Renaissance Middle', '3911', 1, 'A ''B'' rated Middle School committed to developing inquiring, knowledgeable, and caring global learners by providing a rigorous, IB focused curriculum that ensures high school readiness, fosters academic and intellectual potential, and promotes social-emotional growth in a safe, inclusive environment, preparing students for success in a changing world.', '2025-12-11 10:00:00-04', null),
(151, 'New Renaissance Middle', '3911', 2, 'Innovative Verizon Innovative Learning Lab Students participate in rigorous Project-Based Learning experiences that incorporate Augmented reality, 3D-Printing, and robotics, effectively blending academic standards with creativity.', '2025-12-11 10:00:00-04', null),
(151, 'New Renaissance Middle', '3911', 3, 'Diverse Extracurricular Opportunities Cavaliers participate in a wide range of clubs and activities, including Dance, Peer Counseling, Drama, SGA, NJHS, and Debate, fostering leadership and engagement.', '2025-12-11 10:00:00-04', null),
(151, 'New Renaissance Middle', '3911', 4, 'Our students achieve an impressive 93% success rate on the Biology EOC and 90% in Algebra and Geometry, earning valuable high school credits while in middle school.', '2025-12-11 10:00:00-04', null),
(151, 'New Renaissance Middle', '3911', 5, 'Academic Acceleration Our school offers various acceleration opportunities for students, enabling them to gain an early start on high school credits through courses like Algebra, Geometry, Biology, Spanish I and II, and career technical courses.', '2025-12-11 10:00:00-04', null),
(151, 'New Renaissance Middle', '3911', 6, 'Diverse academic, arts, leadership, and athletic programs with free after-school opportunities that help students learn, lead, and thrive.', '2025-12-11 10:00:00-04', null),
(152, 'Bennett Elementary', '0201', 1, 'We’re proud to announce that Bennett Elementary has earned a ‘B’ school rating—just one point away from an ‘A’! This achievement reflects the hard work and dedication of our students, staff, and community.', '2025-12-11 10:36:00-04', null),
(152, 'Bennett Elementary', '0201', 2, 'Bennett Elementary is honored to be recognized as a Special Olympics National Banner Unified Champion School—a distinction that celebrates our commitment to inclusion, respect, and leadership through unified sports and activities', '2025-12-11 10:36:00-04', null),
(152, 'Bennett Elementary', '0201', 3, 'Bennett Elementary offers seven unique clubs that inspire creativity, leadership, and collaboration. Students can explore their interests through Readers Theater, Technology Club, Student Council, Debate, LEGO Club, Art Club, and the Safe Promise Club', '2025-12-11 10:36:00-04', null),
(152, 'Bennett Elementary', '0201', 4, 'Our school offers dynamic STEM-focused Science Specials for 5th grade students, providing hands-on learning experiences that deepen scientific understanding and spark curiosity through exploration.', '2025-12-11 10:36:00-04', null),
(152, 'Bennett Elementary', '0201', 5, 'Bennett Elementary offers a Debate program for 4th and 5th grade students, helping them build confidence and public speaking skills. Our team proudly competes in tournaments across the district throughout the year.', '2025-12-11 10:36:00-04', null),
