(244, 'Mirror Lake Elementary', '1841', 1, 'Strong Student Growth Trends  PM2 data reflects positive academic gains across multiple grade levels, with notable growth in Kindergarten, 2nd, 3rd, and 5th grades, and continued upward progress in 1st and 4th grade.', '2026-04-09 10:12:00-04', '2026-04-14'),
(244, 'Mirror Lake Elementary', '1841', 2, 'Commitment to Equity & Inclusion  Mirror Lake proudly serves a diverse student population and remains committed to equity through intentional instructional practices that ensure access, representation, and success for all learners.', '2026-04-09 10:12:00-04', '2026-04-14'),
(244, 'Mirror Lake Elementary', '1841', 3, 'Targeted Support for All Learners  Strategic interventions for SWD and ELL students, including Walk to Read and daily targeted instruction, ensure individualized support and accelerated growth.', '2026-04-09 10:12:00-04', '2026-04-14'),
(244, 'Mirror Lake Elementary', '1841', 4, 'Collaborative & Dedicated Staff  A unified team of teachers, coaches, and support personnel work collaboratively to meet students’ academic and social-emotional needs while maintaining high expectations and a strong culture of care.', '2026-04-09 10:12:00-04', '2026-04-14'),
(244, 'Mirror Lake Elementary', '1841', 5, 'Data-Driven Instructional Practices  Instruction is driven by consistent data analysis, allowing teachers to differentiate instruction, monitor student progress, and adjust teaching strategies to meet learner needs in real time.', '2026-04-09 10:12:00-04', '2026-04-14'),
(244, 'Mirror Lake Elementary', '1841', 6, 'Clear Instructional Framework  The implementation of the Gradual Release of Responsibility Model supports student mastery by moving learning from teacher modeling to guided practice and independent application.', '2026-04-09 10:12:00-04', '2026-04-14'),
